+   "rule": "The stat sheet (brief 080; replaces the counted hit outside the fight lab). A shot's chance is a sum anyone can read: aim (by class, plus the character's `offset`, 0 for now) + range (point inside weapons.pointBlank, eff inside the weapon's effective ring, long to its max) + cover (the target still beside cover, in its arc, past point blank: full or partial; a running target past point blank takes targetRunning in its place) + movement (the shooter walking, running or running away, and pinned), kept between limit.min and limit.max. Each shot draws once, from the shooter's own stream (seed/id/shot, by its shot number), hit or miss; damage is the weapon's, fixed, no criticals; a read of the odds never draws. Streaks lean the player's way, and the how-to-play says so: after streak.hits in a row from one hostile on one agent, the next misses; after streak.misses in a row from one agent on one target, the next hits, if the chance is streak.floor or more. One agent takes at most one hit every `intake`, whoever is firing: focus fire lands fast, never faster, and a shot inside the gap misses (it draws all the same). A miss never hits anyone else. Enforcer at warnHealth or below: the warning, once (enforcer.warning, Game.EnforcerWarnedAt). weapons.acc and weapons.mod now serve only the fight lab and test-only pre080 runs. Guards walk and run back at guardSpeed; every other pace is unchanged." },
