-  "rule": "Who carries what and how a shot lands (Sky 2026-10-15, briefs/011/motive-fights.md). The Enforcer carries the carbine (the cell's); every other operative may carry a pistol, one per `sidearmArms` of Arms (the Handover issues all three); the guard, the patrol, officers and rivals carry pistols; the Enforcer, officers, the guard and the patrol are trained. A shot's accuracy is its band's (inside `pointBlank`, inside the weapon's eff, inside its max) times each modifier that applies, in per mille: the shooter's gait this tick (tuning.md §8.3, Sky 2026-10-21: a walk `mod.moving`, a run toward or across `mod.running`, a run away, its step within `runAwayCone` degrees of straight away from the target, `mod.runningAway`), the target still beside cover (`mod.cover`; with `pointBlankCover` false, never inside `pointBlank`: Sky 2026-10-21, tuning.md §8.4, as the lab) or, for a target running this tick past point blank, `mod.targetRunning` in its place (one step, never with cover), the Enforcer holding Vale (`mod.vale`), an untrained shooter (`mod.untrained`). Hits are deterministic: each shooter keeps an integer accumulator on each target, the pair's for the mission (tuning.md §13.1, engine 0.18.0, as the lab's aim memory): taking a target resumes the count the shooter left on it and nothing resets it (a switch, cease, hold, holster, a release); a target it has not fired at starts at `acc.start`; each shot adds the accuracy, and at 1000 or more the shot hits and 1000 comes off (750: exactly three in four). A shot does the weapon's damage; health per kind is `health`, at 0 down. The cost moves from the shot to the victim: +`costs.gunfire` T once per shooting (the first shot at each target, hit or miss), +`costs.hit` T per person hit, once, and +`costs.down` more when they go down; the final fight stays untraced (fight.traced). A drawn weapon seen by security raises Alert to `costs.drawSeenSecurity` and that watcher engages; seen by people, it is one witnessed incident (Alert at least `costs.drawSeenPeople`, standing per traceable weapon-drawn), and drawings within `costs.drawWindow` and witness range of it are the same incident (Motive addendum 2026-10-15). Fire on the move (tuning.md §8.2): a fire order stops a walker (it stands and fires, or walks in when out of reach or line) and never stops a runner (the run goes on, firing at its gait; out of reach it walks in once the run ends); a driven agent keeps its drive and fires at each tick's gait; a move given while a fire order stands keeps the order and fires on the move, and spends its walk-in (out of reach when the move ends, it holds its aim `lineLapse` and lapses; a new fire order walks in again); stances fire at the gait's chance. Engine 0.21.0 (Sky 2026-10-22, brief 041: \"Keep them firing until out of range I would say, same for running\"): a lasting fire order (the fire order, a lock, a focus) that has had its target in reach (the weapon's max ring) and line on some tick ends at once when the target is beyond that ring, whether the agent walks, runs, is driven or stands, or the target moves (log fire.out-of-range; no walk back in, no lapse); a new act (an order that engages the agent: watch, listen, turn, call, loop, reroute, mislead, takedown, carry, drop, stash, restrain, enter, take, board) ends it (log fire.cancelled); until it has had reach and line, the walk-in and the lapse above stand. Anyone can be shot (tuning.md §9, Sky 2026-10-21) but the cell's own agents. Orders: draw (`draw` ticks), holster (`holster`), stance (hold, return, free), fire until down (first shot `aimNew` after taking the target; holds aim `lineLapse` when the line breaks), cease, panic (once a fight is on). A civilian or a contact is a target only when the order says so (the host's right hold and the ring's Fire always say so, brief 041: the hold is the confirmation). Tuning.md §9 (engine 0.15.0): Vale, a final-fight hostile after fight.over, a knocked-out or restrained person where they lie (a hit kills them: a takedown kill's consequences plus the gunfire's), a response unit or robot by its own id and a camera (\"camera:<id>\", `health.camera`; shot out it is dark for the mission; gunfire only: no hit or down Trail, no Standing) are all targets; a person shot down outside the final fight lies dead where they fell (a brief-013 body); the cell's own agents are the one target refusal (fire-on-cell). An order whose shot would fail the mission (Vale; the driver while Vale is out) always takes the `costs.loudHold` hold. Brief 030 (Sky 2026-10-20): `close`: a fire order on a target out of the weapon's reach, or with no clear line, walks the grid (at a walk) to the nearest free point inside its effective reach with a clear line (within 60 m of walk; none: refused out-of-range or no-clear-line), stands there and fires; it holds while it walks (no lapse), and a driven agent is not walked (the host drives; the order holds). `autoHolster`: a weapon drawn by a fire order or by panic (not by a draw order) is holstered by the engine `autoHolster` seconds after the fight it was drawn for ends (fight.public: quiet after its last shot, the final fight at fight.over), unless the agent still has a fire order, a stance order was given since the draw, or a hostile combatant up within its weapon's max reach has a clear line to the agent (then at the first tick none has); a weapon drawn with a draw order stays drawn until holstered.",
