-  "footprint": { "len": "v:car-len-cm", "w": "v:car-w-cm", "clear": "v:car-clear-cm", "reach": "v:car-reach-cm", "rule": "A standing car is ground nobody walks through (engine 0.33.1; brief 041, Sky playing 0.2.122: \"characters are walking through cars\"). Every car the mission simulates (car:getaway, car:official, car:rivals; the range's spawned cars) blocks, while it stands, the walk cells whose centres lie within its footprint (`len` along its heading, `w` across, centred on the car's point) grown by `clear` on every side; while it drives it blocks nothing. It stands at a stand or a bay, at its stops, parked, waiting with Vale, stopped where its driver went down or where it was disabled, and as a wreck. Its heading is the one the host draws: the getaway car its stand's facing, the official car its bay's long axis at the pickup (site car.blockFacing) and car.serviceFacing in the service bay, the rival car its stop's facing (rivals.car.facing), a stopped car the way it was driving. Every walk made while it stands goes round it (the walk grid's A* on the free cells it leaves; the grid's own cells never change): a walk that would end on its ground ends at the free cell nearest that point and steps in from there (a person getting into the car), and a walk from inside it (getting out) starts at the free cell nearest. A move order to its ground ends at that free cell (no step in). When a car comes to stand, whoever stands on its ground steps to the free cell nearest, and a walk in hand that would cross its ground is walked again round it, to the same end, from where the walker is (engine 0.36.0, brief 079; an operative mid-act stays, his act holds him). The response unit's walk, made once at load, goes round the mission's start cars. At the car is within `reach` of its body (no longer at-reach-cm of its centre): Board and a rival reaching Vale at the getaway car. A disabled official car's people stand beside it across its heading, the driver on the road side and Vale on the kerb side. The crowd's routine legs go round the cars standing when each leg sets out (read at the start of the tick): the legs built at load go round the mission's start cars (the getaway car at its first stand, the official car at the pickup); once a car stands elsewhere a leg that would cross it is walked again round the cars standing then." },
