 its centre): Board and a rival reaching Vale at the getaway car. A disabled official car's people stand beside it across its heading, the driver on the road side and Vale on the kerb side. The crowd's routine legs go round the cars standing when each leg sets out (read at the start of the tick): the legs built at load go round the mission's start cars (the getaway car at its first stand, the official car at the pickup); once a car stands elsewhere a leg that would cross it is walked again round the cars standing then." },
   "pickup": { "valeIn": "v:vale-in-s", "rule": "Vale's car at the official bay (brief 059 K1–K4; GDD v0.25.0 §07; Sky's answer 3a). Vale always walks from the official door to his car (5:50 to 6:10) and gets in `valeIn` later. Unturned, his driver drives him away then: the mission fails vale-leaves. Turned, the driver drives him round to the service bay along the drive grid at car.pace (car.parks when it stops) and waits there with Vale in the back until the mission's close (schedule.over), whatever his day in the people file says; at the close, if no Take has begun, he drives Vale on and the mission fails vale-leaves. A Take begun before the close holds him until it ends. With no driver (down) the car waits and Vale stands by it. A Take at his car is in-car (no struggle, nothing to witness) only with the driver turned and the car parked round the back; at the front with a turned driver it is refused (driver-brings-vale), and while the car is driving round (car-not-parked). The driver's Call (the camera block) is retired (Motive M059-6.1)." },
