   "openRule": "Sky's open questions from brief 059 (decision log 23–25), each a value: S1 is answered (Sky 2026-10-25: no, the final fight always comes): the value fight-always, its rule in alwaysRule (fight.safe.leaveUnfought is retired into it: 1 is the old false and more, 0 the old true); S2 `loud.entry` (nearest, Sky 'yea': the loud fight's officers come from whichever of the response unit's entry (site fight.entry) and the mission's official entrances (the world's entrances of kind official) is the shortest grid walk to the getaway car's stand; response: always the response unit's entry); S3 the value rivals-follow-cm-s (280, run, Sky; the walk is 160).",
   "alwaysRule": "The final fight always comes (Sky's S1; Motive briefs/059/motive/s1-rulings.json M059-S1.2 to S1.5; GDD v0.25.0 §06, §07). With safe.always 1: (1) the gate: from the final fight's start until it is over, Go with Vale aboard is refused (car-held) while the fight's blocker is not out (down or gone). The blocker holds the car wherever he stands while he is up, not only on his lane post. Before a blocker is named, whoever is coming holds it: car:rivals while a member still rides in the rival car (the refusal's tick is the first step-out), a member walking back or due to wake (safe), or the officers on their way (loud). The hold within fight.hold or on the exit lane applies on top as always. Go without Vale (withdrawing by car) and the menu's Withdraw are not gated. (2) The late spring: the ambush springs as built (the Enforcer with Vale, not inside, within safe.ambush of the stand's car) or once Vale is in the car; the blocker is picked at the spring from the crew on foot, and if none is on foot then, at the tick the first one steps out, among those on foot (shortest walk, ties by id); each later arrival alerts as he steps out and fires weapons.aimNew after. (3) The floor (safe.floor): at the safe fight's start, count the members able (alive and not bound: a knocked-out one due to wake counts) and coming (on foot, in the rival car, or due back). If fewer than safe.floor, away members come back, the earliest at the stand first (ties by id), until the count reaches the floor or nobody away is left: the tipped car cuts its tip short, re-enters at rivals.car.entry and rides to the stand's rival stop, where the wheelman steps out `out` s later; the warned lookout walks back from rivals.posts.lookoutExit to his spot (rivals.recalled). Nothing spawns; a killed or bound member stays gone. (4) Crew destroyed: with no member able at the fight's start (all killed or bound, none recalled), the safe fight is over at once (rivals.wiped, fight why crew-destroyed) and the gate is open. 0 turns (1), (3) and (4) off: a cell gone before anyone holds the car leaves unfought (engine 0.32.0).",
