ts, (a), (b), Withdraw, or (loud) the seal. The walk is the fight AI's own movement (an advance to a point), not a routine.",
-  "spacing": { "clear": "v:body-clear-cm", "file": "v:body-file-ticks", "rule": "Nobody in a fight stands in anybody else (engine 0.36.0; brief 079, Sky: \"Rivals were overlapping each other\"). Two bodies may pass; where a body's walk ends, or where it stands with none, it claims. The bodies: a final-fight body, a member of the rival crew on foot, the response unit, a police unit, and an operative on the street (the operatives' own moves stay the player's: this rule never moves one). A walk that would end within `clear` of another's claim ends at the free walk cell nearest that place clear of every claim, and outside the car's hold and lane unless the place itself was inside (a blocker's lane point stays his; a walk to a car's door ends at the car). A stand or spot found taken this way gives way to that cell, which is the body's stand from then on. A body that stops mid-walk on another's claim takes the step to such a cell, firing as it walks. Officers sent in together from one entry come in file, `file` apart. A claim is read from the walks and stands already in the state, so nothing new is hashed and the same orders give the same places." },
