+  "spacing": { "clear": "v:body-clear-cm", "file": "v:body-file-ticks", "cell": true, "rule": "`cell` (engine 0.37.0, brief 081; proposed, Motive to confirm): an operative's move that would end within `clear` of a claim ends at the free cell nearest it clear of them all, beside the person, not in them. Claims also take the guard, the patrol at rest off its sweep, the waitress and the driver at their places; every response officer spreads the same way as it sets out. Nobody in a fight stands in anybody else (engine 0.36.0; brief 079, Sky: \"Rivals were overlapping each other\"). Two bodies may pass; where a body's walk ends, or where it stands with none, it claims. The bodies: a final-fight body, a member of the rival crew on foot, the response unit, a police unit, and an operative on the street. A place within the getaway car's Board reach stays within it. A walk that would end within `clear` of another's claim ends at the free walk cell nearest that place clear of every claim, and outside the car's hold and lane unless the place itself was inside (a blocker's lane point stays his; a walk to a car's door ends at the car). A stand or spot found taken this way gives way to that cell, which is the body's stand from then on. A body that stops mid-walk on another's claim takes the step to such a cell, firing as it walks. Officers sent in together from one entry come in file, `file` apart. A claim is read from the walks and stands already in the state, so nothing new is hashed and the same orders give the same places." },
